{
  "id": "27883_wazurau",
  "headword": "患う",
  "reading": "わずらう",
  "romaji": "wazurau",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to suffer from (an illness); to be ill",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to suffer from (an illness); to be ill",
      "explanation": "To be afflicted with a disease or long-term medical condition. More formal and literary than {病気|びょうき}になる, and usually implies a serious or prolonged illness."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "27883_wazurau_ex1",
      "japanese": "{長|なが}く{患|わずら}っている。",
      "english": "He has been ill for a long time.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27883_wazurau_ex2",
      "japanese": "{父|ちち}は{心臓|しんぞう}の{病|やまい}を{患|わずら}っていた。",
      "english": "My father suffered from a heart condition.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "27883_wazurau_ex3",
      "japanese": "{大病|たいびょう}を{患|わずら}ってから、{健康|けんこう}の{大切|たいせつ}さを{知|し}った。",
      "english": "After suffering a serious illness, I came to understand the importance of health.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY:\n- Transitive ({他動詞|たどうし}); the illness is marked with を.\n- Pattern: [illness]を{患|わずら}う\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {病|やまい}を{患|わずら}う: to suffer from a disease\n- {大病|たいびょう}を{患|わずら}う: to suffer a serious illness\n- {長年|ながねん}{患|わずら}う: to be ill for many years\n\nNOTE: As a verb suffix, わずらう attaches to the masu-stem to mean \"have trouble doing,\" as in {思|おも}い{煩|わずら}う (to fret) or {言|い}い{煩|わずら}う (to struggle to say).",
